i\fake a quart of good, well-steeped tea. Then take a large punch-bowl
and put in three-quarters of a piut of cognac, one-quarter of :1 pint of Jamaica
rum, the fresh juice of four lemons and six heaping teaspoonfuls of sugar. Set
this mixture on fire and stir rapidly, adding the hot tea slowly the while.
